## 4. Source Code Availability

When you Distribute the Software or a Derivative Work in a form other than Source Code, you must also make the corresponding Source Code available to recipients under this License.

The Source Code must be provided in a reasonably accessible and machine-readable form.

You may satisfy this requirement by:

* distributing the Source Code together with the Software;
* providing a publicly accessible location from which the Source Code can be obtained without additional licensing fees; or
* providing another reasonable method through which recipients can obtain the complete corresponding Source Code.

The Source Code must include the material necessary to build or reproduce the distributed version, including applicable build scripts, configuration files, and other project-specific material reasonably required for that purpose.

This requirement does not extend to operating-system components, standard libraries, compilers, interpreters, or other generally available software that is not itself part of the Software.

