## 6. Preservation of Attribution

Attribution is a fundamental condition of this License.

When you Distribute the Software or a Derivative Work, you must preserve all existing:

* copyright notices;
* author names;
* developer names;
* contributor names;
* organization names;
* attribution statements;
* attribution files;
* historical contribution records; and
* other notices identifying previous developers or contributors

that were included with the version of the Software from which your work was derived.

You may not remove, obscure, replace, falsify, or deliberately diminish such attribution.

### 6.1 Previous Developers

A person identified in an Attribution Record as a developer or contributor remains entitled to attribution in subsequent versions of the Software.

A subsequent developer may not remove that person's attribution merely because the subsequent developer has substantially rewritten, reorganized, renamed, or replaced portions of the Software.

The fact that a previous developer no longer participates in development does not by itself permit their attribution to be removed.

### 6.2 New Contributors

You may add your own attribution to the Software.

You may add yourself, your organization, or other legitimate contributors to the Attribution Record when appropriate.

Adding new attribution must not replace or subordinate the attribution of previous developers or contributors.

### 6.3 No False Attribution

This License does not require anyone to claim that a previous developer created, reviewed, approved, or contributed to modifications that they did not actually make.

Attribution must accurately describe historical contributions.

A Modified Version must clearly distinguish its modifications from the original work.

### 6.4 Attribution Files

If the Software contains an `AUTHORS`, `CONTRIBUTORS`, `NOTICE`, `CREDITS`, or equivalent file, every Distributed Derivative Work must preserve that file or an equivalent record containing all existing attribution information.

Additional contributors may be appended to such a record.

Existing entries may not be removed merely because a later developer considers them obsolete, inconvenient, or unnecessary.

### 6.5 User Interfaces

If the Software provides an interface containing an appropriate location for legal notices, the Software must preserve reasonable attribution information there when the original Software provides such information.

This requirement does not require an interface to display an impractically large list of historical contributors where an accessible credits or attribution section is reasonably available.

